{
  "$schema_note": "Shared test vectors for the L1 rental rate optimizer (blueprint \u00a72.2). APPEND-ONLY with stable ids \u2014 a changed expectation must be a loud diff, never a silent edit. Both the canonical TS implementation (shared/rental-rate-math.ts) and the SQL mirror consume this file; divergence fails the build gate. All money is integer CENTS. Formulation: minimize 28m*month + 7w*week + d*day subject to 28m+7w+d >= billable_days (COVERAGE, overshoot allowed). Tie-break: fewest segment lines, then largest blocks first. 'fired' means the optimum STRICTLY beat (> 0 cents; ties never fire) the greedy largest-block exact partition (months, then weeks, then days) \u2014 that partition is the 'beaten_alternative' a meter-style biller would have charged, and the only legal basis for a printed savings line. Duration resolution (off-rent clock, grace, minimums, calendar rules) is a SEPARATE stage with its own vector set \u2014 billable_days arrives here pre-computed.",
